-| Python required | 3.12 or newer (`requires-python`). 3.12 is the lowest version the package allows; the full test suite was run on 2026-11-12 on earlier commits of this repository (not on the commit that holds this file): Windows with Python 3.13 reported 2449 passed, 15 skipped; Linux with Python 3.12 (a container) reported 2462 passed, 2 skipped; no test failed on either. These are run results of those earlier commits; no log of either run is shipped and they were not repeated on this commit. The skipped tests need another operating system, a tool that machine did not have, or the load measurement. Edits were made after those runs, including a Semgrep workflow, a lock file and test files, and these counts do not cover them. The one measured fact for this commit: `python -m pytest --collect-only -q` (collection only, no test run; Linux, Python 3.12.3, no network) prints one line per test file, in the form `tests/test_workflow_run_flags.py: 10` (that is its last line), 91 lines in all, and the counts on them add up to 3726 (added up by hand from those lines; the command prints no total). This is a count of listed tests, not a run result. | pyproject.toml |
+| Python required | 3.12 or newer (`requires-python`). 3.12 is the lowest version the package allows; the full test suite was run on 2026-11-12 on earlier commits of this repository (not on the commit that holds this file): Windows with Python 3.13 reported 2449 passed, 15 skipped; Linux with Python 3.12 (a container) reported 2462 passed, 2 skipped; no test failed on either. These are run results of those earlier commits; no log of either run is shipped and they were not repeated on this commit. The skipped tests need another operating system, a tool that machine did not have, or the load measurement. Edits were made after those runs, including a Semgrep workflow, a lock file and test files, and these counts do not cover them. The one measured fact for this commit: `python -m pytest --collect-only -q` (collection only, no test run; Linux, Python 3.12.3, no network) prints one line per test file, in the form `tests/test_workflow_run_flags.py: 10` (that is its last line), 92 lines in all, and the counts on them add up to 3883 (the per-file counts added up from those lines; the command prints no total; counted on 2026-11-13 on the tree of public main f3c39cf8 with the documentation changes applied, which add no test file and no test). This is a count of listed tests, not a run result. | pyproject.toml |
